// P03.20 (R12): a runaway generic instance graph.
// satisfiesClone walks the graph of types with an explicit stack: no
// recursion, so a deep type cannot overflow the stack, and no depth cut, so
// the depth of a type never decides the answer. Each generated case runs
// under `timeout 3` (a quadratic or exponential walk fails it) and reports
// exactly the errors checked here, so a false error fails it (and a crash
// fails any RUN line, also under `not`). Split by case so each test stays
// well under the 2 s budget in the ASan build (D0.13).
//  - runaway: T[int] would reach ever larger instances T[Option[...[int]]]: an
//    instantiation cycle (P03.23). It is one error at the declaration, the
//    type is invalid, and the 100 Clone() calls add nothing (the walk bound
//    of P03.20 is gone).
//
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-strict-stress.py 0 walk runaway > %t.ra.gopp
// RUN: not timeout 3 %gopp check -check-j=1 --check-error-limit=0 %t.ra.gopp > %t.ra.out 2>&1
// RUN: grep -c "error\[E" %t.ra.out | FileCheck --check-prefix=ONE %s
// RUN: grep -c "error\[E0366\]: instantiation cycle" %t.ra.out | FileCheck --check-prefix=ONE %s
// ONE: {{^1$}}
package main
